    "governingPrinciples":  [
                                "Payment and fulfillment are separate concerns.",
                                "A successful payment must not itself be treated as proof that fulfillment completed.",
                                "A fulfillment operation must have an explicit product identity, order identity, customer delivery destination, fulfillment state, and delivery result.",
                                "Fulfillment must be safe to retry without accidentally creating uncontrolled duplicate delivery behavior.",
                                "Provider-specific payment payloads must be normalized before entering the fulfillment domain.",
                                "The product artifact delivered to a customer must be derived from an explicitly approved product release artifact, not directly from an arbitrary working-tree manuscript.",
                                "The private source manuscript must not become publicly addressable merely because commerce is implemented.",
                                "A customer must not receive access before the corresponding purchase has reached an authorized paid state.",
                                "Fulfillment failures must remain observable and recoverable rather than silently losing a paid order.",
                                "No implementation may claim that delivery exists until an end-to-end fulfillment path has been verified."
                            ],
